    "summary": "9 specs filed before `verify` existed (007, 021, 032, 034, 038, 039, 040, 041, 042) sit on the legacy ledger in `scripts/verify-sweep.sh` with no executable acceptance, although the tests that hold their behavior exist and pass. This spec carries that acceptance for them under `amends_verification`, the route spec 132 used, and deletes their ledger lines in the same change. Every command names its tests exactly and asserts the exact pass count, so a renamed or deleted test turns the block red instead of passing on an empty filter. The area is verdicts, attestation, lifecycle leniency, governance documents and the PyPI shim.\n",
